{"name":"Suede Leather","hex":"#896757","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"suede","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of soft leather, made from calfskin, with a brushed texture to resemble fabric, often used to make boots, clothing and fashion accessories."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of suede."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suede"},{"term":"leather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tough material produced from the skin of animals, by tanning or similar process, used e.g. for clothing; often denotes leather from cattle when no qualifier specifies otherwise.","A piece of the above used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of leather.","Referring to one who wears leather clothing (motorcycle jacket, chaps over 501 jeans, boots), especially as a sign of sadomasochistic homosexuality."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Suede","blocks":[{"text":"Suede is a type of leather with a fuzzy, napped finish, commonly used for jackets, shoes, fabrics, purses, furniture, and other items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Blue_suede_samba.JPG/330px-Blue_suede_samba.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suede"},{"title":"Leather","blocks":[{"text":"Leather is a strong, flexible and durable material obtained from the tanning, or chemical treatment, of animal skins and hides to prevent decay. The most common leathers come from cattle, sheep, goats, equine animals, buffalo, pigs and hogs, ostriches, and aquatic animals such as seals and alligators."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Leathertools.jpg/330px-Leathertools.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leather"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip